/* ============================================================
   Status-indicator  (from snippets/Status-indicator.reference.html)
   Aria: aria-hidden, role="status", aria-live
   Reuses: used as the status detail in List items transaction rows — same tint-chip primitive
   Finding: rag/warning dot = 1.69:1 on white (< 3:1) — meaning carried by the label (1.4.1); use the tint chip (form B) when warning must stand alone. NOT declared as a passing pair.
   Finding: rag/neutral-tint missing from the store — neutral/cancelled has no chip form (token gap; add rag/neutral-tint to complete the RAG tint set)
   Finding: PASSIVE atom: no hover/active/keyboard by design (anti-pattern to make it interactive); AT = role=status + aria-live (4.1.3) + label (1.4.1)
   Finding: s212-D2 (Dave, #212) — the G17 RAG status manifestation canon set is A+B+C. Mapping onto this snippet: G17-A = the inline dot+label (form A above, unchanged); G17-B = the FILLED CELL (new, salience-ramp fill rung, for status columns in dense tables); G17-C = the BAR / edge accent (new, for cards and grouped rows). Tags and pills stay EXCLUDED from status (ctkt / ctkt-018) and are not drawn here. NAMING HAZARD: this snippet's pre-existing form A/B/C labels are a DIFFERENT taxonomy (inline / tint chip / live-announced) minted 2026-06-22 — the G17 letters are prefixed G17- everywhere to keep the two apart.
   Finding: G17-B neutral/cancelled has NO fill leg: rag/neutral has no -background sibling, the same shape as the rag/neutral-tint gap above. The cancelled row falls back to the inline dot+label rather than inventing a fill token.
   Finding: G17-B per-theme ink, MEASURED (base gate resolves the mono store only, so these are recorded here): mono err 5.55 / warn 7.99 / ok 10.59 / info 7.04; legacy err 7.87 (guard: white, s131-D1) / warn 10.28 / ok 4.56 / info 7.17; console err 6.02 (guard: white) / warn 6.95 / ok 7.65 / info 4.61 (guard: on-light); supercharge err 6.02 (guard: white) / warn 7.53 / ok 7.65 / info 4.99 (guard: on-light). The console+supercharge INFO guard is PROPOSED, NOT RULED — see the theme override $note.
   Finding: G17-C carries no new declared pair: the edge is a 4px accent, not the carrier — the label inside the bar carries the meaning (icon-013 / 1.4.1), exactly as the dot does. The warning edge is the same sub-3:1 value as the warning dot and is likewise NOT declared as a passing pair.
   Scope: .cn-status-indicator   ============================================================ */
.cn-status-indicator{
  --font: "Univers Next for HSBC","Helvetica Neue",Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
  --ease: 140ms ease;
  --success: var(--rag-success);
  --warning: var(--rag-warning);
  --error: var(--rag-error);
  --neutral: var(--rag-neutral);
  --info: var(--rag-information);
  --success-tint: var(--rag-success-tint);
  --warning-tint: var(--rag-warning-tint);
  --error-tint: var(--rag-error-tint);
  --info-tint: var(--rag-information-tint);
  --err-bg: var(--rag-error-background);
  --warn-bg: var(--rag-warning-background);
  --ok-bg: var(--rag-success-background);
  --info-bg: var(--rag-information-background);
  --on-dark: var(--rag-text-on-dark);
  --on-light: var(--rag-text-on-light);
  --on-ok: var(--text-on-success);
  --on-info: var(--rag-text-on-information);
  --surface: var(--surface-subtle);
  --label: var(--text-default);
  --disabled: var(--text-disabled);
